## Why This Is Asked
Validates understanding of tenant isolation, least privilege principles, and comprehensive auditing in serverless architectures.

## Key Concepts
- IAM condition-based per-tenant isolation
- CMK encryption with tenant-specific key policies
- DynamoDB partition access patterns by tenant namespace
- CloudTrail immutability for audit integrity
- API Gateway context propagation for tenant identity

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example policy snippet (pseudo)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["dynamodb:GetItem","dynamodb:PutItem"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:dynamodb:*:*:table/tenant-data",
      "Condition": {
        "ForAllValues:StringEquals": {
          "dynamodb:LeadingKeys": "${aws:userid}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests cross‑account trust, least privilege, and basic auditability in a concrete, beginner‑friendly scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Cross‑account IAM roles
- Trust policy and restrictive permissions
- DynamoDB granular access
- STS session duration and credential rotation
- Auditing with CloudTrail

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "RoleName": "LambdaToAccountBLogsRole",
  "AssumeRolePolicyDocument": {
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [
      {
        "Effect": "Allow",
        "Principal": {"Service": "lambda.amazonaws.com"},
        "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
      }
    ]
  },
  "Policies": [
    {
      "PolicyName": "DynamoDBPutItem",
      "PolicyDocument": {
